# Atlas RCP — project rules

## Language & direction
- Arabic is the DEFAULT locale. Every screen must work perfectly in RTL first,
  then LTR.
- Never use physical CSS properties for layout spacing. Use logical properties
  only: ms-/me-/ps-/pe-, start-/end-, text-start/text-end, border-s/border-e.
  `ml-4` and `left-0` are bugs.
- Set <html lang={locale} dir={locale === 'ar' ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'} translate="no">.
  The `translate="no"` is mandatory — browser auto-translation corrupts
  regulatory Arabic terminology.
- NEVER hardcode user-facing strings. Every string goes through next-intl.
  Both ar.json and en.json must be updated in the same change.
- Numbers, dates and currency use Intl with the active locale. Currency is SAR.

## Brand tokens — use these, never invent colours
Defined as CSS variables in globals.css:
  --atlas-green: #519E53        primary
  --atlas-green-600: #3E7C40    hover/pressed
  --atlas-green-300: #6BB56D    light accent
  --atlas-green-tint: #EEF5F0   section wash
  --ink-900: #1C2229
  --ink-800: #252821            body text
  --ink-500: #4D4D4D            secondary text
  --line: #DDDDDD               hairline borders
  --surface: #FFFFFF
  --surface-alt: #F7F9F7
Status semantics (deliberately NOT brand green, so a passing state is never
confused with a brand element):
  --state-ok: #1F7A4D
  --state-bad: #B3261E
  --state-warn: #B45309
  --state-neutral: #6B7280
  --state-info: #2563EB
  --state-gap: #7C3AED

## Typography
- Display + body: Montserrat Arabic, Montserrat (matches atls.com.sa).
- Data/utility: IBM Plex Mono — used for request numbers, invoice numbers,
  hashes, INS codes. Monospace signals "machine-verified value".
- SELF-HOST all fonts via next/font/local. Never fetch a font from a CDN at
  runtime. This is a hard rule.

## Visual language
- Flat surfaces. Hairline 1px --line borders. Border radius 8px (12px for cards).
- No gradients, no drop shadows beyond a single subtle elevation token.
- One accent colour on screen at a time.
- Generous whitespace; density only in data tables.
- Motion: 150-200ms ease-out. Respect prefers-reduced-motion. No decorative
  animation.

## Copy rules
- Active voice. A button says exactly what happens: "Submit request", not "OK".
- An action keeps the same name through the whole flow: the button that says
  "Return to client" produces a toast that says "Returned to client".
- Errors state what happened and what to do next. Never surface a raw upstream
  error string to a user.
- Empty states are an invitation to act, with the primary action inline.

## Engineering rules
- Server Components by default; "use client" only where interactivity requires it.
- All mutations are Server Actions in src/server/, validated with a Zod schema
  at the boundary. Never trust client input.
- Every query that touches tenant data MUST filter by the caller's
  organisationId. Write a `scopedDb(session)` helper and use it everywhere.
- Authorisation is checked server-side on every action via `requirePermission()`.
  Hiding a button is not authorisation.
- Money is Prisma Decimal, never float. Format only at render time.
- Every state transition writes an AuditLog row. No exceptions.
- No `any`. No unhandled promise. No console.log in committed code.
